@@ -130,6 +130,25 @@ The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each hold
 
 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+The clinic publishes the same veterinarian-and-specialty relationship from the specialty side as well. One page lists every specialty the clinic knows, each under the name it is stored as. Under each specialty are the veterinarians who hold it, given by full name — first name then last name `[REQ-VET-003]`. This page is the specialty directory, not the veterinarian directory: a veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on it. However many specialties the clinic knows, they all appear on the single page rather than a page at a time. The page reads the existing directory only; nothing on it adds, changes, or removes a veterinarian or a specialty (NG-2).
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed under the name it is stored as.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty one or more veterinarians hold, when the specialty directory is opened, then each of them is shown under it as first name then last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given more specialties than fit one screen, when the specialty directory is opened, then all of them are on that one page and no page-at-a-time control is offered.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty no veterinarian holds is still listed, showing no veterinarian under it.
+2. The specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+3. A veterinarian holding more than one specialty appears under each of them.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
